WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.000
(music)

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.820
I''m Mike McGehee and I'm a Professor in
Materials Science Engineering at Stanford University.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.200
I'm also a senior fellow in
the Precourt Institute for Energy.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.200
And I am the director of the Energy
certificate program.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.400
I have a degree in physics from Princeton University

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.300
and a PhD in materials science from University of California, Santa Barbara.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:39.100
Ah, when I was a graduate student, ah, I saw the opportunity to apply to be a professor at Stanford.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.300
I was initially disappointed because it was my dream job and I thought I was too young but I went for it

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:54.610
I applied and I got it. And here I am. I find solar cell
research to be fascinating because there

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:01.260
are so many different possible solutions
to the problem. And as someone who's been

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:07.149
working in the field for over 15 years I
know my mind has been changed several

00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:12.780
times on what the most promising
approach is. Ah, my lab works on several

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.670
different kinds of solar cells. We take a
holistic view towards it and study

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:25.189
everything from how they're made, to how
they work, to ah, what they would cost. And we

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:29.200
tried interact with industry to make sure
we're developing effective solutions.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.990
(music to fade out)

